Export PriorityQueueSender/Receiver on Android.

What: compile gpui's `queue` module and re-export `PriorityQueueSender` and `PriorityQueueReceiver` when
`target_os = "android"`, next to the existing windows/linux/wasm cfgs. Cfg-only; no change on other targets.

Why: Parallax's Android dispatcher (parallax-android) runs GPUI on the Android main Looper and uses the same
priority queues as the Linux and Windows dispatchers for its main-thread queue and background pool, instead of
reimplementing GPUI's priority handling. Android's target_os is "android", not "linux", so the existing cfg misses it.

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

